  "reason": "With only one data point (config_005: multimodal/multiprofile/scgpt/imagenet_vit_l/transformer/concat at 0.507 acc), the most fundamental uncertainty is whether the multimodal architecture is actually necessary or whether a single modality could be competitive. config_014 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, transformer) directly tests the contribution of the image modality while holding the RNA encoder (scgpt) and aggregation (transformer) constant. If RNA alone approaches 0.507, it signals the image branch isn't adding value and I should redirect my remaining 7 experiments toward RNA optimization or image-only variants. If RNA alone is substantially lower, it confirms multimodal is the right direction and I can confidently exploit the multimodal space for the rest of the budget. This is the highest-information experiment at this early stage because it resolves the most consequential design-axis question before committing further budget to fine-grained multimodal ablations."
}

